:09] - [01:14]: \"Okay, on this app, there are physical relationships, friends, etc.\" -> This is a description of the app's nature or a general statement. It's not a proposal for a sexual act or a request for nudity. It's more of a general observation.\n    *   [01:14] - [01:17]: \"So, they do meet up, like that.\" -> Again, talking about what *others* do on the app (\"they\"). This falls under \"Stories and reported speech\" or general observation. Not a direct proposal to meet.\n    *   [01:20] - [01:30]: Asking if they are a friend. Ordinary conversation.\n    *   [01:31] - [02:12]: Dinner talk, hometown (Bangalore), work (insurance). Ordinary conversation.\n    *   [02:12] - [02:40]: Marriage talk, talking about time and changing behavior. Relationship talk (Allowed).\n    *   [02:44] - [03:00]: \"I'm busy\", \"you should be a good friend\". Ordinary conversation.\n    *   [03:04] - [03:20]: Dinner talk, \"call me after having dinner\". \"Call me\" inside the app is allowed.\n    *   [03:25] - [03:55]: Food talk, tailoring work, call disconnecting. Ordinary conversation.\n\n    *   *PlatformMove?* No requests for WhatsApp, Telegram, phone numbers, or specific proposals to meet the other person. (Mentioning \"they do meet up\" is general/reported).\n    *   *SuspiciousActivity?* No mention of money, rates, or payments for sexual services.\n    *   *Explicit-Flirting?* No requests for nudity, sexual acts, \"open talk\", or \"non-veg talk\". Relationship talk (\"girlfriend\", \"married\") is explicitly allowed.\n\n    *   The conversation is very mundane. It's mostly small talk about dinner, work, and relationship status.\n    *   The mention of \"physical relationships\" and \"meet up\" at [01:09] is a general statement about the app's users (\"they\"), not a direct request to the other person. According to the \"About a Violation\" section, stories or reported speech (what people do) are not violations.\n\n    *   Since no violations were found, the output shoul